  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 305-10-05, a deposit in transit is cash the company has recorded as a debit to its Cash account but that the bank has not yet processed or credited. This item is added to the bank balance during reconciliation because the company mailed the deposit before the bank''s cutoff.
Wrong (A): A wire transfer to a foreign bank describes an outgoing payment, not an incoming deposit recorded by the company awaiting bank credit.
Wrong (C): An NSF check is a book-side adjustment that reduces the company''s cash balance, not a deposit awaiting bank processing.
