  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 480-10-25-4, mandatorily redeemable financial instruments must be classified as liabilities because they embody an unconditional obligation to transfer assets at a specified date. The $1,100,000 redemption amount is reported as a liability, not equity.
Wrong (A): Permanent equity classification is reserved for instruments without mandatory redemption features; the obligatory repurchase removes the residual-interest characteristic of equity.
Wrong (C): Mezzanine equity applies to conditionally redeemable instruments outside the issuer''s control, not to instruments with unconditional mandatory redemption.
Wrong (D): There is no temporary equity classification under GAAP for instruments with fixed mandatory redemption dates; ASC 480 requires immediate liability treatment.$EXPL$
